# piiscrub environment variables
# MVP: none required

# Where fetch-dataset.sh reads corpora from and where `make corpus` writes its
# converted datasets. OPTIONAL — it defaults to testdata/external, which
# .gitignore excludes, so leaving it unset is the normal case. Set it only when
# the corpora live somewhere else (for example on a shared machine). The value
# is used by scripts/fetch-dataset.sh, the Makefile's DATA_ROOT, and
# tools/corpusbench.
# DATAPROTECT_DATA_DIR=testdata/external

# v2+ (future):
# PII_SCRUB_MIN_CONFIDENCE=0.7
# PII_SCRUB_NLP_MODEL_PATH=./models
# PII_SCRUB_FACE_MODEL_DIR=./models/dlib
# PII_SCRUB_API_ADDR=:8080
# NLP sidecar (see docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-20-nlp-sidecar.md):
# PII_SCRUB_NLP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8787
# Managed NLP sidecar: set this INSTEAD of PII_SCRUB_NLP_URL (setting both is an
# error). The value is the path to the piiscrub-sidecar binary; the library
# starts it on a free loopback port and stops it on Close. Read by
# nlp.ManagedFromEnv(), not by nlp.FromEnv().
# PII_SCRUB_NLP_BINARY=/path/to/piiscrub-sidecar
# Opt-in card-label language for scripts/benchmark.sh only (comma-separated
# checksum.Language codes, e.g. sv). Unset scores with the English default.
# PII_SCRUB_CARD_LANG=sv
# LLM second pass (t7-phase-2): optional local judge for weak candidates
# (e.g. bare 12-digit MyKad). Set PII_SCRUB_NLP_JUDGE_URL to enable; the judge
# runs on a local OpenAI-compatible endpoint bound to loopback. The model name
# defaults to qwen3-0.6b (Apache-2.0).
# PII_SCRUB_NLP_JUDGE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8788
# PII_SCRUB_NLP_JUDGE_MODEL=qwen3-0.6b
# Set to 1 to allow non-loopback URLs (not recommended; the context window is PII).
# PII_SCRUB_NLP_JUDGE_ALLOW_REMOTE=1
